
 1. savannah hardcoded out of the hub filter (config agent)                                                                        
  workflow_builder.py hardcodes only atlanta and jacksonville in the Filter_Leads WHERE clause. savannah is in values.yaml and
  Python's filter_agent.py reads it correctly — but the hub Logic App silently drops every Savannah lead. This has been broken since
   the city was added to the YAML.                          
                                                                                                                                    
  2. Handle_Outreach_Error doesn't catch Gemini failures (arch agent)                                                               
  Call_Gemini_Outreach is missing from the spoke's Handle_Outreach_Error.runAfter. If Gemini fails on the outreach call and exhausts
   retries, the spoke exits without writing outreach_skipped=true or any error marker. That lead sits forever in a "classification  
  complete, outreach pending" ghost state with no visibility.
                                                                                                                                    
  3. Deployed workflow JSONs are stale (config agent)       
  deploy/workflows/hub-workflow.json still has outputs('Parse_Classify_Args')?['source_id'] as the RowKey in
  Upsert_Classification_To_Table — the old bug. workflow_builder.py was already fixed in this session but sync.py --apply was never 
  run. Azure is still running the broken version.
                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                       
  HIGH — Structural Gaps
                        
  4. Contact dict not normalized before use (pipeline agent)
  _build_user_content in base.py uses contact.get("dm_requested") etc. directly from Gemini's output. Optional fields Gemini omits  
  produce None in the prompt string (dm_requested=None). If Gemini returns contact as null entirely, it falls back cleanly — but    
  optional-field None leaks into the prompt and can confuse the spoke's Gemini call.                                                
                                                                                                                                    
  5. Classifier batch is all-or-nothing (pipeline agent)                                                                            
  If Gemini returns zero tool calls (policy block, malfunction, etc.), _parse_tool_response raises ValueError that propagates all
  the way up — the entire batch of leads fails with no per-lead fallback. One bad response loses everything in the batch.           
                                                            
  6. Hub has no classification error handler (arch + data agents)                                                                   
  If Call_Gemini_Classify exhausts all retries, the lead row has stored_at/content/authorName but no classified_at, no category, no
  spoke call — and no error flag. No recovery path, no way to detect it programmatically.                                           
                                                            
  7. Idempotency broken on duplicate webhooks (data agent)                                                                          
  Duplicate delivery of the same lead ID overwrites stored_at (masking original receipt time), can change category if Gemini is
  non-deterministic, and can convert an Others row to an actionable one, firing a second spoke. No first-seen-at guard or ETag      
  protection.
                                                                                                                                    
  ---                                                       
  MEDIUM — Operational Quality
                                                                                                                                    
  8. Others + error rows write sparse columns (data agent)
  Upsert_Others_To_Table and Handle_Outreach_Error only write 3 fields (outreach_skipped, errorMessage, outreach_at). The other 5   
  columns (is_complete, missing_fields, outreach_message, investment_summary, location_insights) are absent — not null, literally   
  missing from the entity. Any downstream reader needs to defensively handle absent columns.
                                                                                                                                    
  9. Outreach dispatcher is fully sequential (pipeline agent)
  5 leads × ~5s/call = 25s of blocking sequential Gemini calls. The classifier sends all leads in one batch. The outreach dispatcher
   doesn't.                                                                                                                         
   
  10. Parse fallback looks identical to genuine incomplete (pipeline agent)                                                         
  When _parse_response hits tier-3 fallback (raw text as outreach_message), it stores is_complete=false, missing_fields=[] —
  indistinguishable from a real incomplete result. An API error or rate limit message gets stored as if Gemini analyzed the deal and
   found it lacking.                                        
                                                                                                                                    
